"""Human part 78a: the campaign files (game/campaign.cpp lines 81-108, 114-281, 308-320, 414-465, 531-563, 576-618,
634-644, 677-800, 870-979: the nodes' LoadDefinition, Load and Save, the containers' children, C_Campaign's LoadFiles,
Clear, the definition parsers, the destructors), against the original's.

Run with the campaign's build (campaign/build_campaign.bat): MUT_HARNESS=campaign, MUT_BAT=build_campaign.bat,
MUT_WRAPPER=campaign_diff.cpp (it includes the mutated source), MUT_EXTRA_SRCS _re/harness/collision/original_exe.cpp,
MUT_EXTRA_INC _re/harness/collision;_re/harness/interface, MUT_LDFLAGS -Wl,--image-base=0x20000000, HD2_CAMPAIGN_QUICK=1
in the environment (and the game data: HD2_UNPACKED, default H:\\HD2_Unpacked).
Labels: G + the line. Generated by part 61's scratch generator (gen_mutations.py's kinds, plus names and constants swapped
for their partners (the campaign's own list), && / ||, string literals; each line's text widened until found once in the
file).

Result (2026-11-21): 424 mutants, 64 not building; 291 of the 360 building killed, 69 survived, all equivalent or out of
the comparison's reach:
- The nodes' return values (G 125, 136, 139, 163, 171, 229, 241, 251, 269, 279, 445, 464, 538, 553, 607, 617, 699, 702,
  708, 742, 781, 799, 931, 951, 957, 977 bool): no caller reads them.
- The loops' HasMore() back to RemainingSize() > 0 (G 145, 180, 200, 259, 417, 545, 595, 710, 748, 933, 959 code): they
  differ only once a read has run past its chunk; files that do it (a chunk's size grown past its container or into its
  sibling) make both read strings of no bytes, where the original shows the string read before (its reader does not end
  the buffer), or loop for ever: not compared.
- Memory freed or not (G 310 del, G 316 del/code: Clear's deletes, the front one twice a double delete the harness does
  not see; G 641 num, G 642 del, G 872 num, G 873, 874, 875, 881, 911 del).
- ReadChunkString's buffer and its end (G 97 num, G 99 cmp/num, G 101 del/num: the strings compared are ended; 0 bytes
  read either way); LoadFiles' path buffer (G 894 num); initial values a successful read overwrites (G 188, 219, 536,
  686, 903 num).
- Null checks of pointers no caller passes null (G 707, 930, 956 and); the play's LoadDefinition (G 733 del: it reads
  nothing); m_unknownF0 (G 883 del: nothing sets it).
- Ascend and Close that Close or the destructor repeat (G 905 del: the version chunk's, the reader one level deeper
  with nothing read past it; G 921, 924 del); the definition strings' Ascend when their chunk is of another id (G 588,
  701 del: the chunk's text then read as chunk headers, a damaged file).
"""
